  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a 111-indexed string SSS of length NNN containing lowercase English letters.\n\nYou also have an initially empty string AAA.\n\nRepeat the following process until SSS is empty:\n\n\nFind the lexicographically maximal substring of SSS;\nLet it be S[l..r]S[l..r]S[l..r], where 1≤l≤r≤∣S∣1 \\le l \\le r \\le |S|1≤l≤r≤∣S∣ and ∣S∣|S|∣S∣ denotes the current length of SSS (if there are multiple occurrences of the maximal substring, you may choose any of them);\nAppend this substring to AAA, i.e. set A:=A+S[l..r]A := A + S[l..r]A:=A+S[l..r], where +++ denotes string concatenation;\nDelete S[l..r]S[l..r]S[l..r] from SSS and concatenate the remaining parts, i.e. set S:=S[1..l−1]+s[r+1..∣s∣]S := S[1..l-1] + s[r+1..|s|]S:=S[1..l−1]+s[r+1..∣s∣] (note that one or both of these substrings may be empty).\nOutput the value of AAA at the end of the process.\n\nIt can be proved that the output is unique.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN.\nThe second line of each test case contains a lowercase English string SSS of length NNN.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the value of string AAA at the end of the process.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1051 \\le N \\le 5 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤5⋅105",
      "SSS consists of lowercase English letters, i.e, the characters `a` through `z`.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n7\nabacaba\n4\nbabc",
        "output": "cababaa\ncbab",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The process takes three steps:\n\nThe lexicographically maximal substring of \"abacaba\" is \"caba\" with l=4l = 4l=4, r=7r = 7r=7.\nAAA becomes \"caba\", SSS becomes \"aba\".\nThe lexicographically maximal substring is \"ba\" with l=2l = 2l=2, r=3r = 3r=3.\nAAA becomes \"cababa\", SSS becomes \"a\".\nThe lexicographically maximal substring is \"a\" with l=1l = 1l=1, r=1r = 1r=1.\nAAA becomes \"cababaa\", SSS becomes empty.\n\nThe final value of ttt is \"cababaa\"."
      }
    ]
  },
